      "description": "We're building a simple parser for a CMS and need to detect opening HTML tags for a div element. The tag must start with '<div' followed by optional attributes (each attribute is a name, optionally an equals sign and a quoted value) and end with '>'. Attribute names must be letters, digits, hyphens, underscores, or colons, starting with a letter or underscore. Quoted values can use either single or double quotes and may contain anything except the quote character. Whitespace is allowed between attributes and before the closing '>'. The tag must be matched in isolation (the entire input string).",
