      "slot": 1,
      "description": "Our internal file upload service only accepts files located under /var/www/uploads or its subdirectories. We need a client-side check that tells the user their path is valid if and only if it starts with exactly that prefix followed by either nothing or a slash, and after that any sequence of path components separated by single slashes is allowed. Each component may consist of letters, digits, underscores, hyphens, dots, or spaces, but may not be empty (so no double slashes, no trailing slash unless the path is exactly the prefix). The whole path must be absolute and start with a slash.",
