    {
      "slot": 4,
      "description": "A Unix absolute path must satisfy all of the following: (1) start with a forward slash; (2) after the initial slash, the path is a sequence of one or more components separated by single forward slashes; (3) each component may contain letters, digits, underscores, hyphens, dots, and spaces; (4) no component may be empty, so the path must not contain consecutive slashes; (5) the path must not end with a slash; (6) the path must not contain the special components '.' or '..' as a whole component, e.g. '/foo/./bar' and '/foo/../bar' are invalid; (7) the path must not contain any whitespace at the very beginning or very end (spaces inside components are allowed); (8) the path is considered case-sensitive. Reject any path that fails any rule.",
