      "slot": 1,
      "description": "Our build script needs to verify that every JavaScript file contains a properly formed ES module import statement from the React package, appearing at the start of a line (allowing leading whitespace). The statement must be of the form `import` followed by whitespace, then either a default import name or a named import block, then whitespace, `from`, whitespace, then a quoted string that is exactly 'react' (single or double quotes), and finally a semicolon. For the default or named import parts, use the standard restrictions: a default import is a valid JavaScript identifier (letters, digits, underscore, dollar sign, not starting with a digit). A named import block is a comma-separated list of one or more identifiers, with optional spaces around commas, enclosed in curly braces. The default import can be combined with a named import block, separated by a comma. Do not allow side-effect imports (no import clause before 'from'). Whitespace can be spaces or tabs.",
      "regex": "/^[ \\t]*import[ \\t]+(?:[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*(?:[ \\t]*,[ \\t]*\\{[ \\t]*[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*(?:[ \\t]*,[ \\t]*[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*)*[ \\t]*\\})?|\\{[ \\t]*[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*(?:[ \\t]*,[ \\t]*[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*)*[ \\t]*\\})[ \\t]+from[ \\t]+['\"]react['\"];[ \\t]*$/m"
    },
    {
      "slot": 2,
      "description": "A TODO or FIXME comment line in a source file must match the following format: optional leading spaces or tabs, then `//`, then optional spaces or tabs, then either `TODO` or `FIXME` (in uppercase), then optional spaces or tabs, then an optional colon `:`, then optional spaces or tabs, and finally any non-empty message text. The message text can be any characters except newline. The line should be considered in a multiline context.",
      "regex": "/^[ \\t]*\\/\\/[ \\t]*(?:TODO|FIXME)[ \\t]*:?[ \\t]*\\S.*$/m"
    },
    {
      "slot": 3,
      "description": "Match a line that is a comment starting with two slashes, followed by optional spaces or tabs, and then the word TODO, FIXME, or NOTE in uppercase. The line may have leading spaces or tabs before the slashes. The whole line must match, with nothing else after the keyword (except possibly spaces or tabs).",
      "regex": "/^[ \\t]*\\/\\/[ \\t]*(?:TODO|FIXME|NOTE)[ \\t]*$/m"
    },
    {
      "slot": 4,
      "description": "Match a comment line that mentions TODO or FIXME anywhere, allowing for any text before or after the keyword. The comment must start with `//` and may have leading spaces or tabs before the slashes. The keyword can be in any case (uppercase, lowercase, or mixed). The rest of the line can be anything except a newline.",
      "regex": "/^[ \\t]*\\/\\/.*(?:TODO|FIXME).*$/im"
    },
    {
      "slot": 5,
      "description": "A CSS class name following the BEM (Block, Element, Modifier) naming convention must be validated. The format is: block, optionally followed by an element and/or a modifier. The block is one or more lowercase letters, digits, or hyphens, but must start with a lowercase letter. An element part is two underscores (`__`) followed by an element name: one or more lowercase letters, digits, or hyphens, starting with a lowercase letter. A modifier part is two hyphens (`--`) followed by a modifier name: one or more lowercase letters, digits, or hyphens, starting with a lowercase letter. The element part, if present, must come before the modifier part. Examples of valid names: `block`, `block__element`, `block--modifier`, `block__element--modifier`.",
      "regex": "/^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(?:__[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)?(?:--[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)?$/"
    }
  ]
}

