      "description": "We need a reminder system where users can type in a simple schedule using a cron-like expression. It should have five fields separated by spaces: minute, hour, day of month, month, and day of week. For minute and hour, allow numbers within their usual ranges. For day of month, allow 1-31. For month, allow 1-12, and also common three-letter abbreviations (jan, feb, ...) case-insensitive. For day of week, allow 0-6 where 0 is Sunday, and also common three-letter abbreviations (sun, mon, ...) case-insensitive. Also, we want to allow a wildcard asterisk for any field, and a step value like */5 in minute/hour to mean every 5 units. Keep it simple—no ranges, lists, or other advanced syntax.",
