      "description": "For our internal router we need to validate relative paths in the admin panel. A path is valid when it begins with a single slash, then has at least one character that is a letter, digit, hyphen, underscore, or period, and may contain multiple such segments separated by single slashes, but it must not end with a slash. Query strings and fragments are not part of this field.",
      "regex": "/^\\/(?:[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\/)*[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 3,
      "description": "Our design system needs to validate the hex color codes used in themes. We only accept short 3-digit or full 6-digit hex colors, with or without a leading hash, and never the 4- or 8-digit alpha forms.",
      "regex": "/^#?(?:[0-9A-Fa-f]{3}|[0-9A-Fa-f]{6})$/"
    },
