{
  "items": [
    {
      "slot": 1,
      "description": "Our desktop app logs the location of user-selected files. We only support files stored on a local drive on Windows, so the path must start with a drive letter (a single letter followed by a colon), then a backslash, then the file name. The file name must end with one of the accepted extensions: .txt, .log, or .md. Any intermediate directories are allowed, each separated by a backslash, but no directory or file name can be empty, and the path must not contain any forward slashes. The drive letter is case-insensitive.",
