      "regex": "/^\\(\\d+(?:\\.\\d{2})?\\)$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 5,
      "description": "Validate a Japanese yen amount. Rules: The amount is a non-negative integer with no decimal part. It may optionally be preceded by a yen sign (¥). If no yen sign is present, the number must not have leading zeros unless it is zero itself. If the yen sign is present, the number must be a non-empty sequence of digits, and may have leading zeros. The number may contain commas as thousands separators only if the yen sign is present; otherwise commas are not allowed. The commas must be placed correctly: groups of three digits separated by commas, starting from the right, and the first group must have one to three digits. No spaces are allowed.",
