      "description": "Our payment system expects the amount field to include the currency code before the number, like \"USD 1,234.56\" or \"JPY 1000\". The currency code must be exactly three uppercase letters, followed by a space, then the amount. The amount can have an optional comma as a thousands separator (only one comma allowed, separating groups of three digits), and an optional decimal part with exactly two digits. The integer part must have at least one digit. For example, \"USD 1,234.56\" is valid, but \"usd 1,234.56\" is not.",
