    {
      "slot": 1,
      "description": "Our test runner should pick up only files that follow our test naming convention. A file is a test file if its base name (the part before the extension) ends with either \".spec\" or \".test\", and the extension is either .ts, .js, .tsx, or .jsx. The base name must have at least one character before the dot that introduces the suffix. The file name must not contain any path separators (forward slash or backslash). The whole string is the file name.",
