      "description": "Validate a common log line from Apache or nginx in combined log format. The line must have these fields separated by single spaces:\n1. Client IP address: four dot-separated decimal numbers (each 0-255) OR an IPv6 address (hexadecimal groups separated by colons).\n2. Identd user: a hyphen or a non-space token.\n3. Authenticated user: a hyphen or a non-space token.\n4. Timestamp enclosed in square brackets: day, month (three-letter abbreviation), year, hour:minute:second, and timezone offset (e.g., +0000). Example format: [10/Oct/2023:13:55:36 +0000]\n5. Request line in double quotes: method (uppercase letters), space, resource path (non-space characters), space, protocol (HTTP/1.0, HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, or HTTP/3).\n6. Status code: three digits.\n7. Response size: digits or a hyphen.\n8. Referrer in double quotes: any characters except double quotes.\n9. User agent in double quotes: any characters except double quotes.\n\nOnly validate the format; do not check if the IP is routable, if the date is real, or if the status code is meaningful.",
      "regex": "/^(?:(?:\\d{1,3}\\.){3}\\d{1,3}|[0-9a-fA-F:]+) \\S+ \\S+ \\[\\d{2}\\/[A-Za-z]{3}\\/\\d{4}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2} [+-]\\d{4}\\] \"[A-Z]+ \\S+ HTTP\\/(?:1\\.[01]|2|3)\" \\d{3} (?:\\d+|- )?\"[^\"]*\" \"[^\"]*\"$/i"
