      "description": "Our analytics dashboard needs to accept numeric inputs from different sensors. The values can be very large or very small, so they must be entered in scientific notation (like a coefficient and a power of ten). A valid entry consists of an optional sign, a non-empty sequence of digits with an optional single decimal point (but not just a decimal point), followed by the letter 'e' (either case), an optional sign, and a non-empty integer exponent. Only the format is checked; the actual magnitude is not restricted.",
      "regex": "/^[+-]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?[eE][+-]?\\d+$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 2,
      "description": "The system must validate numbers that use commas as thousands separators. The format is: an optional minus sign, then groups of exactly three digits separated by commas, with no leading zeros except for the number zero itself, and no trailing commas. The first group may have one to three digits, and subsequent groups must have exactly three digits. The entire string must match this pattern.",
      "regex": "/^-?(?:0|[1-9]\\d{0,2}(?:,\\d{3})*)$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 3,
      "description": "Validate a signed decimal number with an optional fractional part. The number must start with an optional plus or minus sign, followed by either a single zero or a non-zero digit followed by zero or more digits. Optionally, a decimal point followed by at least one digit may appear. Leading zeros (like 00 or 01) are not allowed except for the single digit 0 before the decimal point. The pattern must match the entire string.",
      "regex": "/^[+-]?(?:0|[1-9]\\d*)(?:\\.\\d+)?$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 4,
      "description": "Scientific notation format: an optional sign, followed by a non-zero digit, then zero or more digits, an optional decimal point with at least one digit after it if present, then the letter 'e' (case-insensitive), an optional sign, and one or more digits. The entire string must conform to this format. No leading zeros are allowed in the coefficient's integer part unless it is zero, but here the integer part must start with a non-zero digit.",
      "regex": "/^[+-]?[1-9]\\d*(?:\\.\\d+)?[eE][+-]?\\d+$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 5,
      "description": "octet 0-255 no leading zeros except for zero itself",
      "regex": "/^(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d{2}|[1-9]?\\d)$/"
    }
  ]
}

{
