      "description": "A semantic version string consists of three numeric components separated by periods: major, minor, and patch. Each numeric component must be a non-negative integer without leading zeros (except the number 0 itself). Optionally, a pre-release version may follow, indicated by a hyphen after the patch version. The pre-release version consists of one or more dot-separated identifiers. Each identifier may contain only alphanumeric characters and hyphens, and must not be empty. Numeric identifiers must not have leading zeros. Optionally, build metadata may follow, indicated by a plus sign after the patch or pre-release. The build metadata consists of one or more dot-separated identifiers, each containing only alphanumeric characters and hyphens, and must not be empty.",
