      "description": "Users on Windows can paste a file path that must start with a drive letter (a single uppercase letter from A to Z followed by a colon and a backslash), then one or more path segments separated by single backslashes. Each segment may contain letters, digits, spaces, hyphens, underscores, and dots, but must not be empty and must not end with a dot or space.",
      "regex": "/^[A-Z]:\\\\(?:[A-Za-z0-9 _-]*[A-Za-z0-9_-]\\\\)*[A-Za-z0-9 _-]*[A-Za-z0-9_-]$/"
