      "slot": 2,
      "description": "In our new developer console, we need to validate user-defined variable names. A variable name must not be any of the following reserved words: 'break', 'case', 'catch', 'class', 'const', 'continue', 'debugger', 'default', 'delete', 'do', 'else', 'export', 'extends', 'finally', 'for', 'function', 'if', 'import', 'in', 'instanceof', 'new', 'return', 'super', 'switch', 'this', 'throw', 'try', 'typeof', 'var', 'void', 'while', 'with', 'yield', 'let', 'static', 'enum', 'await', 'implements', 'package', 'protected', 'interface', 'private', 'public'. Also, the variable name cannot be 'arguments' or 'eval'. Assume the name can be any string of letters (both cases) and underscores, but must not be one of these reserved words.",
