      "description": "In our logistics dashboard, we need to validate a date field that follows the ISO 8601 calendar date format. The accepted format is YYYY-MM-DD, where YYYY is a four-digit year, MM is a two-digit month, and DD is a two-digit day. Both month and day must be zero-padded. However, due to a known compatibility issue with legacy systems, dates in the year 0000 are not allowed. Also, dates before 1583-01-01 are rejected because that's when our company started keeping records; only dates from 1583-01-01 onwards are considered valid for our business. Only the format is checked; we do not verify the actual number of days in the month or leap years.",
      "regex": "/^(?!0000-)(?!158[0-2]-)(?:158[3-9]|1[6-9]\\d{2}|[2-9]\\d{3})-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$/"
