      "description": "An ISO 8601 full date is either:\n- A calendar date in the form YYYY-MM-DD, where YYYY is a 4-digit year from 0000 to 9999, MM is a two-digit month from 01 to 12, and DD is a two-digit day from 01 to 31.\n- An ordinal date in the form YYYY-DDD, where YYYY is a 4-digit year from 0000 to 9999 and DDD is a three-digit day-of-year from 001 to 366.\n- A week date in the form YYYY-Www, where YYYY is a 4-digit year from 0000 to 9999 and ww is a two-digit ISO week number from 01 to 53. Additionally, the week date may be followed by a hyphen and a single-digit day number (1-7 representing Monday to Sunday), making the form YYYY-Www-D.\nThe date components must be exactly as specified; no leading or trailing characters are allowed.",
      "regex": "/^(?:\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|\\d{4}-(?:00[1-9]|0[1-9]\\d|[12]\\d{2}|3[0-5]\\d|36[0-6])|\\d{4}-W(?:0[1-9]|[1-4]\\d|5[0-3])(?:-[1-7])?)$/"
