      "description": "Our error monitoring tool ingests log files and needs to spot lines that look like a JavaScript stack trace frame. A frame line starts with optional whitespace, then the word 'at', a space, then a function name (letters, digits, underscores, dollar signs, dots) followed by a space, then an opening parenthesis, then a file path (any characters except closing parenthesis), then a colon, then a line number (digits), then a colon, then a column number (digits), and finally a closing parenthesis. We only need to know if a line contains such a frame, not that it consists solely of it.",
      "regex": "/^\\s*at [\\w$.]+ \\([^)]+:\\d+:\\d+\\)/"
