      "description": "Our internal tool accepts a field that must contain a non-empty list of integer numbers separated by commas, with no spaces allowed anywhere and no comma at the end. Each integer may be negative and may optionally have a plus sign. Negative zero is not allowed; if a sign is present, the digits must not be all zeros. Leading zeros in the digits are not allowed unless the number is exactly zero (with no sign). Examples of valid integers: 0, -1, 42, +17, -9999. Examples of invalid integers: 00, -0, +0, 1., +, -.",
      "regex": "/^(?:0|-?[1-9]\\d*|\\+[1-9]\\d*)(?:,(?:0|-?[1-9]\\d*|\\+[1-9]\\d*))*$/"
    },
