      "slot": 2,
      "description": "We need to validate that a string is a syntactically correct standard Base64 value without padding. The string must consist only of characters from the Base64 alphabet (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, +, /), and its length modulo 4 must not be 1. The empty string is not allowed. For example, a value ending in two characters where the last character is not one of A, Q, g, w (which have zero low bits) is invalid, and a value ending in three characters where the last character is not one of A, E, I, M, Q, U, Y, c, g, k, o, s, w, 0, 4, 8 (which have zero low bits) is invalid. Do not check any checksum; only the format and bit alignment are verified. Standard Base64 padding characters are not allowed.",
      "regex": "/^(?:[A-Za-z0-9+\\/]{4})*(?:[A-Za-z0-9+\\/]{2}[AEIMQUYcgkosw048]|[A-Za-z0-9+\\/][AQgw])$/"
