      "description": "A valid Python version specifier must satisfy the following:\n1. It must consist of one or more version clauses, each optionally prefixed by an operator: ==, !=, <=, >=, <, >, or ~= (the compatible release operator).\n2. Each clause must be followed by a version string containing one to four dot-separated components.\n3. Each component must be either a non-negative integer (no leading zeros allowed except for the single digit 0) or a non-empty alphanumeric string.\n4. The version string may optionally be followed by a pre-release or post-release segment: a hyphen followed by one or more alphanumeric characters, or a plus sign followed by one or more alphanumeric characters.\n5. Multiple clauses, if present, must be separated by a comma and optional whitespace.\n6. Leading and trailing whitespace is not allowed.",
      "regex": "/^(\\s*(==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|~=)\\s*)?((0|[1-9]\\d*|[A-Za-z0-9]+)(\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*|[A-Za-z0-9]+)){0,3})([-+][A-Za-z0-9]+)?(\\s*,\\s*(\\s*(==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|~=)\\s*)?((0|[1-9]\\d*|[A-Za-z0-9]+)(\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*|[A-Za-z0-9]+)){0,3})([-+][A-Za-z0-9]+)?)*$/"
    },
