      "slot": 4,
      "description": "Accept an http or https URL. Must start with either 'http://' or 'https://' (case-insensitive). After the scheme, the host must be a valid domain name: one or more labels separated by dots, each label consisting of letters, digits, or hyphens, and not starting or ending with a hyphen. The top-level domain must be at least two letters. Optionally, a port number may follow (a colon and one to five digits). The path, query, and fragment are optional; if present, each must start with its respective delimiter (/, ?, #) and may contain any characters except whitespace.",
      "regex": "/^https?:\\/\\/(?:[A-Za-z0-9](?:[A-Za-z0-9-]*[A-Za-z0-9])?\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}(?::\\d{1,5})?(?:\\/[^\\s]*)?(?:\\?[^\\s]*)?(?:#[^\\s]*)?$/i"
