      "description": "Validate an email address with a practical, not RFC-complete format. Rules:\n- The local part (before @) must consist of one or more allowed characters: letters (a-z, A-Z), digits (0-9), and the special characters . _ % + -.\n- The local part cannot start or end with a dot, and cannot contain two consecutive dots.\n- The domain part (after @) must consist of one or more labels separated by dots. Each label must start and end with a letter or digit, may contain hyphens in the middle, and must be between 1 and 63 characters long.\n- The top-level domain (last label) must consist of at least two letters (a-z, A-Z).\n- The entire domain must not exceed 253 characters.\n- The entire email address must not exceed 254 characters.",
      "regex": "/^(?=.{1,254}$)(?=.{1,64}@)[A-Za-z0-9!#$%&'*+\\/=?^_`{|}~-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9!#$%&'*+\\/=?^_`{|}~-]+)*@(?:[A-Za-z0-9](?:[A-Za-z0-9-]{0,61}[A-Za-z0-9])?\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}$/"
