      "description": "We need to flag log lines that look like an Apache or nginx access log entry: a client address, an optional proxy chain, a timestamp in brackets, a quoted request line, and a numeric status code. The client address is either four dot-separated numbers or an IPv6 address in colon-separated hex groups. The timestamp is exactly two digits for the day, followed by a slash, three-letter month abbreviation, slash, four-digit year, colon, two-digit hour, colon, two-digit minute, colon, two-digit second, a space, and a timezone of plus or minus followed by four digits. The request line starts with an HTTP method, then a space, then a request target with no spaces, then a space, then HTTP/ followed by a version number, all inside double quotes. After a space comes a status code. The line must be the entire input.",
