{
  "items": [
    {
      "slot": 1,
      "description": "A Python version specifier string must be validated. The specifier consists of an optional series of version specifiers separated by commas and optional spaces. Each version specifier has:\n- An operator, which is one of: ~=, ==, !=, <=, >=, <, >, or ===\n- A version number that starts with an optional 'v' or 'V', followed by one or more digits, then optionally a dot and digits, then optionally a dot and digits, then optionally a dot and digits.\n- An optional local version segment starting with '+' followed by alphanumeric characters and periods.\n- An optional pre-release segment: a hyphen followed by alphanumeric characters and periods.\n- An optional post-release segment: \".post\" followed by digits.\n- An optional development release: \".dev\" followed by digits.\nThe entire specifier must match from start to end. Whitespace is allowed around commas and operators.",
      "regex": "/^\\s*(?:(?:~=|==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|===)\\s*v?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+){0,3}(?:[-+]?[a-zA-Z0-9.]+)?(?:,|\\s*$)|(?:~=|==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|===)\\s*v?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+){0,3}(?:[-+]?[a-zA-Z0-9.]+)?(?:\\s*,\\s*)?)*$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 2,
      "description": "We need to validate the version string our build system outputs for package releases. The version must follow semantic versioning: major, minor, and patch numbers separated by dots, each being a non-negative integer without leading zeros. After the patch, there can be an optional pre-release label: a hyphen followed by one or more dot-separated identifiers, where each identifier is either a number without leading zeros or an alphanumeric string (letters, digits, hyphens). There can also be an optional build metadata part: a plus sign followed by one or more dot-separated identifiers, each consisting of alphanumeric characters (letters and digits) and hyphens. The pre-release and build metadata can appear independently or together, in that order.",
      "regex": "/^(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)(?:-((?:0|[1-9]\\d*|\\d*[a-zA-Z-][0-9a-zA-Z-]*)(?:\\.(?:0|[1-9]\\d*|\\d*[a-zA-Z-][0-9a-zA-Z-]*))*))?(?:\\+([0-9a-zA-Z-]+(?:\\.[0-9a-zA-Z-]+)*))?$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 3,
      "description": "A Python version specifier is a string that describes a range of allowed versions. It is a comma-separated list of one or more version constraints. Each constraint is an operator followed by a version number, where the operator is one of '~=', '==', '!=', '<=', '>=', '<', '>', or '==='. The version number may optionally start with 'v' or 'V', followed by one or more numeric parts separated by dots (each part is one or more digits), up to four parts. After the numeric parts, an optional pre-release (a hyphen followed by alphanumeric characters and periods) or a post-release ('.post' followed by digits) or a development release ('.dev' followed by digits) may appear. Commas separating constraints may have whitespace around them, and the entire specifier may have leading or trailing whitespace.",
      "regex": "/^\\s*(?:(?:~=|==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|===)\\s*v?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*(?:[-+.]?(?:[a-zA-Z0-9]+(?:[.-][a-zA-Z0-9]+)*))?)(?:\\s*,\\s*(?:~=|==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|===)\\s*v?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*(?:[-+.]?(?:[a-zA-Z0-9]+(?:[.-][a-zA-Z0-9]+)*))?)*\\s*$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 4,
      "description": "We need to check that version numbers in our app follow semantic versioning: a major, minor, and patch number separated by dots. Each number is a non-negative integer without leading zeros (unless it is exactly zero). No other characters are allowed.",
      "regex": "/^(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)\\.(0|[1-9]\\d*)$/"
    },
