    {
      "slot": 1,
      "description": "A Docker image reference must match the following rules: it consists of a registry hostname (optional, only when the reference includes a registry), a repository path, and an optional tag. The registry hostname, if present, is a domain name (one or more dot-separated labels, each label starting and ending with an alphanumeric character and allowing hyphens in the middle). The repository path is a sequence of one or more path components separated by forward slashes. Each path component must start and end with an alphanumeric character and may contain lowercase letters, digits, periods, underscores, and double underscores; single underscores and periods are also allowed. Tags are optional and, when present, must be separated from the repository by a colon and must start with a word character (letter, digit, or underscore) and may be followed by up to 127 word characters, periods, or hyphens. The entire reference must not exceed 255 characters. The check is only for format; existence or validity of the image is not verified.",
      "regex": "/^(?:(?:[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]*[a-zA-Z0-9])?)(?:\\.[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]*[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*\\/)?(?:[a-z0-9]+(?:(?:\\.|_|__|-+)[a-z0-9]+)*\\/)*[a-z0-9]+(?:(?:\\.|_|__|-+)[a-z0-9]+)*(?::[\\w][\\w.-]{0,127})?$/"
