{
  "items": [
    {
      "slot": 1,
      "description": "Our support team needs to quickly filter logs for any line that indicates a slow operation. A line is considered slow if it contains a duration value that is greater than one second. Durations are always written as a number (with optional decimal part) followed by a space and then 's', 'sec', 'second', 'seconds', 'ms', or 'milliseconds'. However, only durations that are strictly greater than 1 second count, so '1000ms' or '1s' or '1.000s' are not slow, but '1.001s' or '1001ms' are. Also, the duration must appear as a standalone token (not as part of a larger word or number). The overall line may contain other text before or after the duration.",
      "regex": "/\\b(?:\\d{2,}(\\.\\d+)?\\s*(?:s|sec|second|seconds)|\\d{1,}\\.\\d{1,}\\s*(?:s|sec|second|seconds)|\\d{4,}\\s*(?:ms|milliseconds)|1001ms\\b|\\d{1,3}(?:\\.\\d+)?\\s*(?:ms|milliseconds))/"
