      "description": "A passphrase consists of at least four words separated by single spaces. Words are sequences of letters, digits, or punctuation without spaces.",
      "regex": "/^\\S+(?: \\S+){3,}$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 4,
      "description": "For our internal banking app, users must set a PIN that is 4 to 6 digits long. However, to prevent trivial PINs, all digits cannot be identical. For example, 1234 is acceptable but 1111 is not. (This only checks the format, not any other security checks.)",
      "regex": "/^(?!^(\\d)\\1*$)\\d{4,6}$/"
    },
    {
      "slot": 5,
      "description": "Password rules:\n- Must not contain any whitespace characters.\n- Must not contain the same character three times consecutively.\n- Must be at least 8 characters long.\n- Must contain at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, and one digit.\n- Must not contain the same character three times in a row (including non-alphanumeric).",
      "regex": "/^(?!.*(.)\\1\\1)(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\\d)\\S{8,}$/"
