{
  "items": [
    {
      "slot": 1,
      "description": "In our CI pipeline we need to detect test files so they can be routed to a separate test runner. A test file is identified by its name: it must end with a dot, then either 'spec' or 'test', then a dot and one of the extensions 'js', 'ts', 'jsx', or 'tsx'. The name before the first dot can be anything (including empty), but the whole file name must be non-empty and may not contain path separators. Case does not matter: '.SPEC.TS' is also a test file. Please check only the file name, not the full path.",
